## Report

**App:** `WebTestBench_0005`, a resume builder — Dashboard, Editor (7 tabs + live preview), 404.

### Screens & components annotated

| Screen | Components |
|---|---|
| Dashboard | `Dashboard.tsx`, `ResumeCard.tsx` (incl. rename + delete dialogs) |
| Editor shell | `ResumeEditor.tsx` (header, title edit, preview toggle, tab bar, 7 panels) |
| Editor tabs | `ContactForm`, `SummaryForm`, `ExperienceForm`, `EducationForm`, `SkillsForm`, `TemplateSelector`, `SectionManager` |
| Preview | `ModernTemplate`, `ClassicTemplate`, `MinimalTemplate` |
| 404 | `NotFound.tsx` |

### Id namespaces

`dashboard.*` · `editor.*` · `contact.*` · `summary.*` · `experience.*` · `education.*` · `skills.*` · `template.*` · `sections.*` · `preview.*` · `notfound.*`

Preview observables reuse the **same `data-semtag-state` keys as the editor inputs** (`contact.email`, `resume.summary`, …), so an agent can link a field edit to its rendered output without extra hints.

### Collections (all verified folding at runtime)

I SSR-rendered every screen and parsed the emitted HTML with an ancestor-stack checker — page-wide id uniqueness, `.item.` ids having a `role="collection"` ancestor, every hinted element having a role, every `select` having options. **All 11 screens clean.** Folds: `dashboard.resumes`→15, `editor.tabs`→7, `experience.list`→20, `education.list`→20, `skills.list`→15, `template.options`→3, `sections.list`→20, `preview.experience`→8, `preview.education`→3–6, `preview.skills`→5.

**Could not fold:** ResumeCard's dropdown menu items, its rename/delete dialogs, and per-skill `SelectContent` options. Radix portals these to `document.body`, outside the collection ancestor, and they only mount while open — at most one at a time, so snapshot cost is bounded.

**Also not folded by design:** Classic renders skills as one joined string, so it uses `preview.skills.names` (observable) rather than a collection.

### Deliberately unhinted

`NavLink.tsx` (unused), all 49 `src/components/ui/*` primitives (hints belong at call sites — verified each spreads `{...props}` so attributes reach the DOM, no prop-widening needed), decorative icons, layout wrappers, positional labels, drag handles.

### Checks

- **Validator:** 160 hinted elements / 75 files — **0 errors, 15 warnings, 0 info**. All 15 warnings are the intentional identical ids across the three preview templates, which are *mutually exclusive at runtime*; template-scoped ids would have been worse (the agent would need to know the active template to read content). This is precisely the blind spot the validator documents.
- **Type-check:** clean. **Build:** passes; **CSS bundle hash unchanged (`index-DNg1yfAr.css`, 67.81 kB)** — zero styling drift. JS 471.47 → 488.44 kB.
- **Lint:** 4 errors + 8 warnings, all **pre-existing** (in `Dashboard.tsx`, `ui/textarea.tsx`, `tailwind.config.ts`). The only diff vs. baseline is one `prefer-const` error shifting line 27→34 because I added the `sortOptions` array above it.

The diff contains attribute changes plus three small non-attribute additions, each required by the spec: `sortOptions` and `skillLevels` arrays (so a select's `data-semtag-options` is built from the same source that renders its items, per §3) and an `itemId` const in `ResumeCard`.

